{
  "version": 1,
  "questionId": "t07-q01",
  "speechText": "Basically, I retry only temporary failures, such as a timeout or a short network problem. I set a retry limit and use exponential backoff, so each attempt waits longer. For invalid input, permission errors, or bad configuration, I fail fast instead of retrying. If a retry could repeat a business action, I make that action idempotent. When an external service keeps failing, I also use a circuit breaker to stop calling it for a short time. This keeps our API from waiting for repeated timeouts and gives the other service time to recover. Later, the circuit breaker lets a small number of requests through to check whether the service is healthy again. So retries handle short failures, while the circuit breaker protects us from a longer outage.",
